艾琳解开了她的谜题，他们已经进入了第二个线索，就在达里尔办公室的音响上。

899
00:42:58.600 --> 00:43:01.420
Craig as Daryl is so funny in this scene.
克雷格饰演的达里尔在这个场景里太搞笑了。

900
00:43:01.420 --> 00:43:05.300
And he's like, pick it up, pick it up, pick it up, pick it up, pick it up, pick it up, pick it up.
他一直在说，拿起来，拿起来，拿起来，拿起来，拿起来，拿起来，拿起来。

901
00:43:05.460 --> 00:43:09.160
They're just talking and he's trying to work.
他们只是在聊天，而他正试图工作。

902
00:43:09.160 --> 00:43:13.980
At eight minutes and 58 seconds, we have a sticky quip callback.
在八分五十八秒处，有一个便利贴笑话的回应。

903
00:43:13.980 --> 00:43:17.940
Did you notice the play me is on a sticky quip?
你注意到“play me”写在便利贴上了吗？

904
00:43:18.020 --> 00:43:19.140
It was also on the puzzle.
它也出现在拼图上。

905
00:43:19.320 --> 00:43:20.820
I saw that as well.
我也看到了。

906
00:43:21.560 --> 00:43:25.580
Also in the background over Andy's shoulder is a photo of Daryl and his daughter.
另外，在安迪肩膀后的背景里，有一张达里尔和他女儿的照片。

907
00:43:25.580 --> 00:43:28.660
It is clearly taken from the Christmas episode.
那显然是取自圣诞节那一集。

908
00:43:28.780 --> 00:43:31.400
And I just want to give a shout out to Michael Gallenberg.
我还要特别感谢一下迈克尔·加伦伯格。

909
00:43:31.680 --> 00:43:34.000
He was always thinking ahead.
他总是很有远见。

910
00:43:34.280 --> 00:43:45.460
He would grab people for photos and then he would give those photos to our set decoration team who would place them and personalize people's desks or save it if we ever were to go to Daryl's house.
他会拉着大家拍照，然后把照片交给我们的布景装饰团队，他们会把照片摆出来，个性化每个人的办公桌，或者留着以备我们去达里尔家拍摄时使用。

911
00:43:45.460 --> 00:43:47.500
We would have that picture of Daryl and his daughter.
这样我们就有那张达里尔和他女儿的照片了。

912
00:43:47.700 --> 00:43:48.920
It was just really smart.
这真是太聪明了。

913
00:43:48.920 --> 00:43:55.900
So we talked a little bit with Greg about these scenes where all of the B-roll of Jim and Pam trying to find the places to hook up.
我们和格雷格聊了一些关于这些场景的内容，比如吉姆和帕姆试图寻找亲热地点的那些空镜素材。

914
00:43:56.020 --> 00:44:06.380
And then of this really magical moment where Michael and Holly realize they love each other and they tell each other in front of the whole bullpen and then shake on it.
还有迈克尔和霍莉意识到彼此相爱，并在整个办公区前向对方表白，然后握手定情的那个非常神奇的时刻。

915
00:44:07.020 --> 00:44:09.780
There's a very sweet Michael talking head afterwards.
之后有一个非常甜蜜的迈克尔的采访镜头。

916
00:44:10.120 --> 00:44:11.500
Oh, it's so good.
噢，太棒了。

917
00:44:11.640 --> 00:44:11.980
I know.
我知道。

918
00:44:12.140 --> 00:44:13.660
He says, yeah, whatever.
他说，是啊，随便啦。

919
00:44:13.940 --> 00:44:14.460
No big deal.
没什么大不了的。

920
00:44:14.680 --> 00:44:16.760
Just the hottest girl in the world loves me.
只是世界上最火辣的女孩爱上了我而已。

921
00:44:17.020 --> 00:44:17.360
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

922
00:44:18.080 --> 00:44:19.260
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

923
00:44:19.440 --> 00:44:20.260
I loved it.
我太喜欢了。

924
00:44:20.840 --> 00:44:25.660
Kelly Cantley shared that NBC immediately put that talking head on a coffee mug.
凯莉·坎特利分享说，NBC立刻把那个采访镜头印在了咖啡杯上。

925
00:44:26.260 --> 00:44:26.660
Really?
真的吗？

926
00:44:26.940 --> 00:44:27.160
Yeah.
是的。

927
00:44:27.380 --> 00:44:28.120
Oh, my goodness.
天哪。

928
00:44:28.120 --> 00:44:29.020
I looked for it.
我找过那个杯子。

929
00:44:29.060 --> 00:44:29.860
I couldn't find it.
但我没找到。

930
00:44:29.980 --> 00:44:32.640
But I did find that quote on several things online.
不过我在网上确实找到了印有那句名言的各种商品。

931
00:44:33.260 --> 00:44:38.080
Andy and Erin are going to go into Ryan's little claw fiSt.
安迪和艾琳要进入瑞安的那个小爪子拳头里了。

932
00:44:38.400 --> 00:44:38.780
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

933
00:44:38.960 --> 00:44:41.160
This is the next step in the treasure hunt.
这是寻宝游戏的下一步。

934
00:44:41.160 --> 00:44:47.200
There are these little glow-in-the-dark sticky stars all over the wall, all over the ceiling.
墙上和天花板上到处都是那种夜光贴纸星星。

935
00:44:47.340 --> 00:44:48.260
It's so cute.
太可爱了。

936
00:44:48.260 --> 00:44:49.480
It's very romantic.
非常浪漫。

937
00:44:49.820 --> 00:44:50.320
Very romantic.
非常浪漫。

938
00:44:50.940 --> 00:44:55.220
Kelly shared on the DVD that the glow-in-the-dark stars were actually painted.
凯莉在DVD花絮中分享说，那些夜光星星其实是画上去的。

939
00:44:56.320 --> 00:44:56.840
Yes.
是的。

940
00:44:57.460 --> 00:45:05.560
Randy said that this was really hard to pull off and that the sticky stars were not showing up on camera when they tested it.
兰迪说这很难实现，因为他们测试时，贴纸星星在镜头里根本显现不出来。

941
00:45:05.900 --> 00:45:13.140
And I guess they had to paint over them with a bunch of extra, what do you call it, like glow-in-the-dark paint.
我想他们不得不给星星涂上一层厚厚的，怎么说呢，就是那种夜光漆。

942
00:45:13.400 --> 00:45:16.360
Kelly said she thinks it was special paint like they use on the highway.
凯莉说她觉得那是像高速公路上用的那种特殊涂料。

943
00:45:16.360 --> 00:45:17.120
Yes.
是的。

944
00:45:17.480 --> 00:45:27.500
Randy also said that they had to add tons of extra ultraviolet lights, including a special ring light that went around the lens of the camera.
兰迪还说，他们不得不增加了大量的额外紫外线灯，包括一个环绕在摄像机镜头周围的特殊环形灯。

945
00:45:28.220 --> 00:45:29.520
Just so those would pop?
就为了让它们显眼？

946
00:45:29.740 --> 00:45:30.920
Just so those would pop.
就为了让它们显眼。

947
00:45:31.200 --> 00:45:36.200
They popped in the room, but when they did a camera test of it, you didn't see it the way you wanted.
它们在房间里看起来很亮，但当他们进行摄像测试时，效果并没有达到预期。

948
00:45:36.460 --> 00:45:38.880
So that was like a high-effort gag.
所以那算是一个高成本的视觉梗。

949
00:45:39.200 --> 00:45:39.600
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

950
00:45:39.700 --> 00:45:41.240
When I first saw it, I was like, oh, so cute.
我第一次看到的时候，心想，噢，太可爱了。

951
00:45:41.240 --> 00:45:43.120
I have those in my daughter's room on the ceiling.
我女儿房间的天花板上就有那些。

952
00:45:43.280 --> 00:45:43.680
Yeah.
是啊。

953
00:45:43.820 --> 00:45:44.160
But no.
但不行。

954
00:45:44.480 --> 00:45:45.320
Highway paint, guys.
那是公路标线漆，伙计们。

955
00:45:45.340 --> 00:45:45.980
Highway paint.
公路标线漆。

956
00:45:46.360 --> 00:45:51.600
As Andy and Erin exit Ryan's little office, Jim and Pam were trying to get in there.
当安迪和艾琳走出瑞安的小办公室时，吉姆和帕姆正试图进去。

957
00:45:51.940 --> 00:45:54.960
They were going to have sex in Ryan's office?
他们是打算在瑞安的办公室里做爱吗？

958
00:45:54.960 --> 00:45:55.980
Come on.
得了吧。

959
00:45:56.920 --> 00:46:08.920
I'm personally so glad that Ryan caught them because since, you know, I'm Pam, I really think we would have regretted having sex in Ryan's office.
我个人很高兴瑞安抓住了他们，因为，你知道，我是帕姆，我真的觉得我们要是真在瑞安办公室里做了那种事，肯定会后悔的。

960
00:46:09.240 --> 00:46:12.500
I feel like that's a memory that Jim and Pam did not need.
我觉得那段记忆吉姆和帕姆根本不需要。

961
00:46:13.980 --> 00:46:16.040
Ryan's smug look about it, too.
还有瑞安那副自鸣得意的表情。

962
00:46:16.040 --> 00:46:18.120
Oh, Pam is like so embarrassed.
哦，帕姆看起来尴尬极了。

963
00:46:18.540 --> 00:46:25.400
It turns out that Michael and Holly not doing PDA is more annoying than PDA.
事实证明，迈克尔和霍莉不秀恩爱反而比秀恩爱更让人心烦。

964
00:46:25.740 --> 00:46:26.060
Yeah.
确实。

965
00:46:26.760 --> 00:46:32.500
I love the scene where they are, like, air-groping each other.
我喜欢他们那种隔空摸来摸去的场景。

966
00:46:32.500 --> 00:46:36.340
I'm trying, I will touch you here, but I can't, so I will hold you here and I will touch you here.
我在努力，我会摸你这里，但我不能，所以我会在你这里停住，然后摸你这里。

967
00:46:36.340 --> 00:46:42.000
During this scene, we have our third catch from Daria R.
在这一幕中，我们收到了来自加拿大安大略省达莉亚·R的第三个发现。

968
00:46:42.200 --> 00:46:43.320
in Ontario, Canada.
在加拿大安大略省。

969
00:46:43.320 --> 00:46:45.300
Uh, Daria, thank you.
呃，达莉亚，谢谢你。

970
00:46:45.500 --> 00:46:46.760
You have quite the eye.
你的眼光真不错。

971
00:46:46.940 --> 00:46:49.220
You should be an honorary member of Office Ladies.
你应该成为《办公室女士》的荣誉成员。

972
00:46:49.520 --> 00:46:51.400
And if anything, mom detectives.
如果非要说的话，应该是妈妈侦探团成员。

973
00:46:51.640 --> 00:46:52.800
That's for sure.
那是一定的。

974
00:46:53.400 --> 00:46:59.560
Daria says at 14 minutes and 30 seconds, we can see Angela watering the plants near Michael's office.
达莉亚说在14分30秒时，我们可以看到安吉拉在迈克尔办公室附近浇花。

975
00:47:00.520 --> 00:47:02.740
Dwight used to water the plants in the office.
德怀特以前负责办公室的浇花工作。

976
00:47:02.960 --> 00:47:04.480
Why is Angela doing it now?
为什么现在是安吉拉在做？

977
00:47:04.780 --> 00:47:09.880
Is he lacking on his duties because of volunteering and doing so much as the building owner?
是因为他忙于志愿服务和作为大楼业主的工作，所以疏忽了职责吗？

978
00:47:10.160 --> 00:47:12.400
Did he assign the task to Angela?
还是他把这项任务分配给了安吉拉？

979
00:47:13.100 --> 00:47:14.780
Angela, please speak to the plants.
安吉拉，请跟植物说说话吧。

980
00:47:15.560 --> 00:47:18.880
Well, I share in the commentary that I'm pruning the plants.
嗯，我在评论里分享过，我当时在修剪植物。

981
00:47:18.880 --> 00:47:22.000
Oh, I guess I started watering, then I pruned.
哦，我想我先是浇了水，然后修剪了枝叶。

982
00:47:22.520 --> 00:47:31.160
By the end of the scene, because we did it so many times, I said I actually felt bad because I had pruned all the dead things off, and then I just started picking up new leaves.
到场景结束时，因为我们拍了很多遍，我说我其实感觉很不好，因为我已经把所有枯萎的部分都剪掉了，然后就开始摘新叶子了。

983
00:47:31.360 --> 00:47:31.780
Oh, no.
哦，不。

984
00:47:32.020 --> 00:47:32.980
I felt bad.
我感觉很糟糕。

985
00:47:33.580 --> 00:47:37.300
I love the idea that Dwight and Angela water the plants.
我喜欢德怀特和安吉拉负责浇花这个设定。

986
00:47:37.820 --> 00:47:41.320
It also makes you question, why did Pam's plant die?
这也让人不禁怀疑，为什么帕姆的植物会死？

987
00:47:41.800 --> 00:47:43.720
It doesn't make me question it.
这倒没让我产生怀疑。

988
00:47:43.720 --> 00:47:48.700
It seems very clear that Angela would not water a plant on Pam's desk.
很明显，安吉拉才不会去给帕姆桌上的植物浇水。

989
00:47:49.620 --> 00:47:58.780
Well, Daria, they put me there by the plant because they wanted a wide range of reaction shots to Michael and Holly, and you couldn't see me way in that accounting nook,
好吧，达莉亚，他们把我安排在那棵植物旁边，是因为他们想要捕捉我对迈克尔和霍莉反应的各种特写镜头，而你在会计室那个角落里根本看不见我，

990
00:47:58.820 --> 00:48:00.380
so they pulled me out to the plant.
所以他们把我拉到了植物旁边。

991
00:48:00.820 --> 00:48:03.420
You'll notice Daryl is at front reception as well.
你会注意到达里尔当时也在前台。

992
00:48:03.720 --> 00:48:05.800
Well, I have, I guess, a Fisher tidbit.
好吧，我有一个关于费舍尔的小花絮。

993
00:48:06.140 --> 00:48:06.480
Oh.
哦。

994
00:48:06.620 --> 00:48:09.580
I haven't known where to bring it up, but maybe now's the time.
我一直不知道该什么时候提，但也许现在正是时候。

995
00:48:09.680 --> 00:48:10.800
You know I love a tidbit.
你知道我喜欢听小花絮。

996
00:48:11.160 --> 00:48:15.420
Did you know that there is a restaurant called Public Display of Affection?
你知道有一家餐厅叫“公开秀恩爱”吗？

997
00:48:15.420 --> 00:48:23.580
It's in Brooklyn, New York, and it is described as a trendy, compact eatery serving creative pizzas, vegetable dishes, and salads, plus beer.
它位于纽约布鲁克林，被描述为一家时尚、紧凑的餐馆，供应创意披萨、蔬菜菜肴、沙拉以及啤酒。

998
00:48:24.300 --> 00:48:31.860
Do you feel like you would be obligated to engage in PDA at the restaurant Public Display of Affection?
你觉得在“公开秀恩爱”餐厅吃饭，是不是就必须得秀恩爱？

999
00:48:32.760 --> 00:48:33.780
I'm curious.
我很好奇。

1000
00:48:34.240 --> 00:48:34.760
No.
不。

1001
00:48:35.340 --> 00:48:39.800
Have you ever encountered an awkward PDA moment?
你有没有遇到过尴尬的公共场合亲热时刻？

1002
00:48:40.060 --> 00:48:46.580
I mean, I don't know if it was so much awkward as just the proximity of me next to the person doing it.
我是说，我不知道那算不算尴尬，只是因为我刚好就在那对亲热的人旁边。

1003
00:48:46.960 --> 00:48:48.640
That feels awkward.
那感觉确实挺尴尬的。

1004
00:48:48.800 --> 00:48:49.040
Okay.
好吧。

1005
00:48:49.040 --> 00:48:51.560
Well, I also thought it was kind of sweet.
不过，我也觉得那其实挺甜蜜的。

1006
00:48:51.840 --> 00:48:52.400
Here's the deal.
事情是这样的。

1007
00:48:52.700 --> 00:48:59.920
We were in line to get on a plane, me and Josh, and you know when you get in the, what is that thing that attaches from the side of the building?
我和乔什当时正在排队登机，你知道那种从航站楼侧面连接到飞机上的东西叫什么吗？

1008
00:49:00.240 --> 00:49:01.800
No, not the tarmac.
不，不是停机坪。

1009
00:49:01.960 --> 00:49:02.620
That's what the plane is like.
那是飞机停的地方。

1010
00:49:02.620 --> 00:49:03.860
Oh, that's what the plane is like.
哦，那是飞机停的地方。

1011
00:49:03.940 --> 00:49:08.560
The tunnel that's like got the accordion door that attaches from the wall to the plane.
就是那个有手风琴式折叠门，连接墙壁和飞机的通道。

1012
00:49:08.560 --> 00:49:09.820
Oh, what do they always call that?
哦，大家平时都管那叫什么来着？

1013
00:49:10.240 --> 00:49:11.900
The jetway?
登机廊桥？

1014
00:49:12.100 --> 00:49:12.680
The jetway.
登机廊桥。

1015
00:49:12.880 --> 00:49:13.280
Bridge?
桥？

1016
00:49:13.280 --> 00:49:14.020
The jet bridge?
登机桥？

1017
00:49:15.180 --> 00:49:17.780
I know someone's going to write in and let us know what that's called.
我知道肯定会有听众写信告诉我们那叫什么。

1018
00:49:18.280 --> 00:49:27.780
So when you're in that single file lane, and sometimes whoever's getting on the plane, if they're taking a while, you kind of get stuck in that corridor tunnel thingy.
总之，当你排成单行进入那个通道时，如果前面的人登机慢了，你就会被困在那个走廊通道里。

1019
00:49:27.820 --> 00:49:27.960
Sure.
确实。

1020
00:49:28.340 --> 00:49:33.300
So we're stuck in the corridor tunnel thingy, and there was a couple in front of us.
所以我们被困在那个走廊通道里，前面有一对情侣。

1021
00:49:33.560 --> 00:49:37.900
This was also a flight to Vegas, so maybe this is the tone.
那还是趟去拉斯维加斯的航班，所以也许这就是基调吧。

1022
00:49:38.240 --> 00:49:40.000
Maybe this is the mood people were in.
也许这就是当时人们的心情。

1023
00:49:40.640 --> 00:49:47.320
But the guy just kept putting his hand on her, like, butt cheek and just giving it a little squeeze.
那个男的就一直把手放在女方的屁股上，还时不时捏一下。

1024
00:49:47.540 --> 00:49:50.620
But, like, we'd take a few steps, he'd give her a little squeeze.
我们每走几步，他就捏一下。

1025
00:49:50.820 --> 00:49:53.100
Then we'd take a few more steps, he'd give her a little squeeze.
再走几步，他又捏一下。

1026
00:49:53.540 --> 00:49:56.160
Well, I think we know what he was hoping would happen in Vegas.
好吧，我想我们都知道他希望在拉斯维加斯发生什么了。

1027
00:49:56.160 --> 00:49:57.000
I think so.
我也这么觉得。

1028
00:49:57.140 --> 00:50:01.020
I have one that's sort of, it's an oral PDA.
我也有一个，算是某种“口头”的公共场合亲热。

1029
00:50:01.380 --> 00:50:01.840
What?
什么？

1030
00:50:02.500 --> 00:50:04.080
So last year...
去年……

1031
00:50:04.080 --> 00:50:04.380
What?
什么？

1032
00:50:04.380 --> 00:50:12.420
Yeah, I was, you know, I was skiing with my family, but they're more advanced skiers than I am.
对，当时我在和家人滑雪，但他们的滑雪水平比我高。

1033
